---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {site} from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Plan your visit"><PageIntro title="You are welcome here." label="Plan your visit" description="New to the area? Curious about Orthodoxy? Visiting for the season? Come and see. You don’t need to have it all figured out before you walk through the door."/><div class="wrap page-body"><div class="intro-two"><div class="prose"><h2>Join us this Sunday.</h2><p>The best introduction to Orthodox Christianity is to experience it. Come pray with us, hear the hymns, and discover the life of our parish.</p><p>Our parish welcomes people from many backgrounds. If this is your first Orthodox service, you are welcome to observe and ask questions. Introduce yourself to Father Hans or a member of the parish.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch before you visit <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><img src="/assets/church.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Worshippers gathered in an Orthodox church"/></div><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-panel"><Icon name="clock" size={29}/><h2>Sunday worship</h2><p><strong>Divine Liturgy · 9:30 am</strong><br/>See the calendar for Orthros, weekday services, feast days, and any schedule changes.</p><a class="text-link" href="/calendar/">View service calendar <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><div class="info-panel"><Icon name="pin" size={29}/><h2>Find St. Peter</h2><p>{site.address}<br/>{site.city}<br/>Off US 41, where Fort Myers meets Estero.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.directions} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get driving directions <Icon name="northeast" size={17}/></a></div><div class="info-panel"><Icon name="cross" size={29}/><h2>Questions first?</h2><p>Call the parish office at {site.phone}. For Father Hans, text is the fastest way to get in touch.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Contact the parish <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div></div><div class="faqs"><p class="eyebrow">A little help feeling at home</p><h2>Your first Sunday.</h2><details><summary>Do I need to be Orthodox to visit?</summary><p>No. You are welcome to attend the services and learn about our faith, whether you are exploring Christianity, come from another tradition, or are simply curious.</p></details><details><summary>What is the service like?</summary><p>Orthodox worship engages the senses through prayer, chanting, icons, candles, and incense. You will see people standing, making the sign of the cross, and venerating icons. You are welcome to observe; you do not need to know every custom to attend.</p></details><details><summary>Can I bring my children?</summary><p>Yes. Bring your family. If you have particular questions or need help planning your visit, contact the parish before you come.</p></details><details><summary>May visitors receive Holy Communion?</summary><p>Holy Communion is received by Orthodox Christians who have prepared to receive. If you are visiting or are unsure, speak with Father Hans. Everyone is welcome to attend and pray with us.</p></details><details><summary>I’m moving to Southwest Florida. Can I join the parish?</summary><p>We would love to meet you. Our parish family comes from across the Gulf Coast, including Fort Myers, Estero, Bonita Springs, and Naples. Visit on Sunday or contact Father Hans to introduce yourself.</p></details></div><iframe class="map-frame" src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=St%20Peter%20Orthodox%20Church%207470%20Hickory%20Dr%20Fort%20Myers%20FL%2033967&t=m&z=15&output=embed" title="Map showing St. Peter Orthodox Church at 7470 Hickory Drive in Fort Myers" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe></div></Layout>
